Single-GPU-class inference for DreamZero-DROID (14B) on 48 GB cards.

Measured footprint: weights are 42.70 GiB (DiT 30.70, umt5-xxl text encoder 10.58, CLIP image
encoder 1.18, VAE 0.24). Each inference spikes ~10 GiB transiently, and the KV cache grows ~2.7
GiB per chunk toward a ~6.5 GiB steady state (max_attention_size = 9 blocks x 880 tokens). Stock,
that peaks near 47.5 GiB against ~46.2 GiB usable and OOMs on the third inference of an episode.

Changes:

1. base_vla.py -- route inputs to action_head._device rather than PreTrainedModel.device.
   self.device is next(self.parameters()).device, which aliases the text encoder's
   token_embedding, so parking that encoder on CPU dragged every input to CPU and raised
   "index is on cpu, different from other tensors on cuda:0".

2. wan_flow_matching_action_tf.py -- memoize the prompt embedding (a pure function of the token
   ids) and evict the 10.58 GiB text encoder to CPU.

3. wan_flow_matching_action_tf.py -- evict the CLIP image encoder after the once-per-episode
   encode_image() call; its outputs are cached in clip_feas/ys for the rest of the episode.

Both encoders are pulled back on demand, so a changed instruction or a reset still works. Neither
is torch.compile'd when offloading is on: reduce-overhead captures CUDA graphs holding raw
pointers into parameter storage, which moving those params to CPU would invalidate.

4. Pipeline-shard the last N DiT blocks onto a second GPU (DREAMZERO_DIT_SPLIT=N, default 0 =
   off). Each moved block frees ~0.93 GiB on the primary GPU (weights plus its slice of the KV
   cache). The block loop carries activations across the device boundary -- one transfer per
   forward with a single tail shard, not one per block -- and returns x to the primary device for
   action_decoder/head. _create_kv_caches allocates each block's cache on its own block's device,
   since the cache is a plain list of per-block tensors. This preserves max_chunk_size=4, i.e. the
   trained attention window; the alternative (lowering max_chunk_size) shrinks it and changes
   model behaviour.

5. socket_test_optimized_AR.py -- DREAMZERO_DISABLE_DREAM_VIDEO=1 skips the model's own generated
   "dream" MP4s. That only skips a vae.decode used to write those files; the action path is
   untouched.

Base commit: ab790c198fbce33503358efbbd4187ce9a89adf3

